{"step_index":163,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:41:13Z","thinking":"**Considering graphs with cycles**\n\nConsidering if a graph with cycles could have radius greater than $\\gamma_t$. Realizing adding an edge to a tree, or in general a graph, can only decrease or preserve its radius: $radius(T + e) \\le radius(T)$. Questioning if adding an edge could decrease $\\gamma_t$ faster than the radius. Preparing to run a script to investigate.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python3 -c \"\nimport networkx as nx\nimport pulp\nimport random\n\ndef gamma_t(G):\n    prob = pulp.LpProblem('TDS', pulp.LpMinimize)\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\n    x = {v: pulp.LpVariable(f'x_{v}', cat=pulp.LpBinary) for v in nodes}\n    prob += pulp.lpSum(x.values())\n    for v in nodes:\n        prob += pulp.lpSum(x[u] for u in G.neighbors(v)) >= 1\n    prob.solve(pulp.PULP_CBC_CMD(msg=False))\n    return int(round(pulp.value(prob.objective)))\n\n# Start from trees where r == g\n# Add 1, 2, 3 random edges and check diff\nbest_diff = -999\nfor n in [8, 10, 12]:\n    for T in nx.nonisomorphic_trees(n):\n        if nx.radius(T) == gamma_t(T):\n            # Try adding all possible single edges\n            non_edges = list(nx.non_edges(T))\n            for e in non_edges:\n                G = T.copy()\n                G.add_edge(*e)\n                r = nx.radius(G)\n                g = gamma_t(G)\n                if r - g > best_diff:\n                    best_diff = r - g\n                    print(f'T+1edge: diff={r-g}, r={r}, g={g}')\n                if r > g:\n                    print('COUNTEREXAMPLE!')\n                    exit(0)\nprint('Done T+1edge! Best diff:', best_diff)\n\"","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc","WaitMsBeforeAsync":20000,"toolAction":"Testing T+1edge graphs","toolSummary":"Test T+1edge graphs"}}]}
